      "message": "Rebuilding on a mismatch makes a cache shared between platforms recover, but it can thrash. Take a non-portable library used from both a Linux and a macOS host through one cache. Each host refuses the other\u0027s artifact, rebuilds it and replaces the entry, so every run on either side compiles from source.\n\nPatch set 3 listed this as an open question (\"Whether a cache with one slot per library can hold the artifacts of several platforms at once\"), and patch set 5 dropped it. The new paragraph settles correctness but not this cost. It\u0027s worth keeping the question under Left open, or keying a non-portable entry by its recorded platform values so both versions can stay in the cache side by side.",
